<title>USA: U.S. weekly soybean crush 29,678,000 bushels.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekly soybean crush 29,678,000 bushels.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Oilseed Processors Association weekly soybean crushings by reporting members (crushings/capacity in bu, soymeal exports in short tons):</p>
<p>			 12/25/96    12/18/96	Year-Ago</p>
<p> Crushings	 29,678,000  30,594,000    27,872,000</p>
<p> Meal Exports	 133,832     167,135	     N/A</p>
<p> Capacity-X	34,948,000  34,948,000    33,569,000</p>
<p> Capacity-Y	35,140,728  35,140,728	     N/A</p>
<p>X-Members reporting weekly. Y-Weekly reporters plus members reporting only monthly. N/A-Not Available. Totals may agree due to rounding by NOPA.  </p>
<p>NOPA reported the following soybean crushings and capacity use by state for the week, with comparisons, in bushels:</p>
<p>    CRUSHINGS --   12/25/96    12/18/96     Year-Ago</p>
<p> Illinois	   5,385,000   5,274,000     5,244,000</p>
<p> Ind, Ky, Ohio    5,122,000   5,183,000     4,479,000</p>
<p> Southeast	  4,608,000   4,985,000     4,765,000</p>
<p> South Central    3,174,000   3,181,000     2,617,000</p>
<p> Southwest	  4,167,000   4,072,000     3,637,000</p>
<p> Iowa		 5,340,000   5,608,000     5,187,000</p>
<p> Minn,ND,SD,Mont  1,882,000   2,292,000     1,943,000</p>
<p> Total U.S.	29,678,000  30,594,000    27,872,000</p>
